# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# outputs/ is PARTIALLY tracked. This is deliberate.
#
# Tracked, because the pipeline cannot regenerate them or because the report is
# bound to them: every *_metrics.json, the frozen windows.json and
# target_intervals.json, molecules.json, rollout_bank.json, provenance.json,
# configs_used.json, and the trained head checkpoints (*.pt).
#
# tests/test_report_matches_artifacts.py re-reads those JSON files and asserts the
# numbers appear in reports/pilot_report.md, so dropping them would silently disable
# 16 tests.
#
# The frozen windows.json and target_intervals.json matter most: they were fixed
# BEFORE any guided result was inspected, and regenerating them on different hardware
# could shift them. Carrying them lets the next machine detect that rather than
# quietly re-derive new ones.
#
# Excluded below: the large arrays from scripts/02_generate_trajectories.py, which are
# reproduced deterministically from the pinned model revision and recorded seeds.
# Re-running step 2 of docs/REPRODUCE.md rebuilds them. Committing ~700 MB to avoid an
# hour of GPU time is not a good trade. See docs/KICKOFF_PROMPT.md §1.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
outputs/**/hidden.npy
outputs/**/features.npy
outputs/**/trajectories.json
outputs/**/prefix_token_ids.json
outputs/**/prefix_meta.csv
outputs/**/predictions_*.npz
outputs/**/rollout_arrays.npz
